For search by meaning, the macOS app and the container image carry, and
indexer/fetch_embed.py installs for a clone:
  all-MiniLM-L6-v2 (sentence-transformers; int8 ONNX export by Xenova),
    Apache License 2.0
  ONNX Runtime, MIT License
  tokenizers (Hugging Face), Apache License 2.0
  NumPy, BSD 3-Clause License
Each package's license is in its .dist-info folder; the model's is stated
at https://huggingface.co/sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2.

For .xls and .ppt files, the same places carry:
  xlrd, BSD 3-Clause License
  olefile, BSD 2-Clause License
Their licenses are in their .dist-info folders.

For OCR, the macOS app carries tesseract and the libraries it uses, built
from their sources by deploy/mac/build_ocr.sh:
  Tesseract OCR, Apache License 2.0
  the English model from tessdata_fast, Apache License 2.0
  Leptonica, BSD 2-Clause License
  libpng, PNG Reference Library License version 2
  libjpeg-turbo, IJG License and BSD 3-Clause License
  LibTIFF, LibTIFF License
  libwebp, BSD 3-Clause License, with Google's patent grant
  GIFLIB, MIT License
Their license texts are in Contents/Resources/ocr/licenses in the app.

The Go version of the server (app/bin/studio-server, in the Linux payload,
the macOS app and the container image) is built from server-go/ and carries
beside it:
  ONNX Runtime 1.31.0 (app/lib), MIT License, from Microsoft's release
    archives at a pinned checksum; its license and third-party notices are
    in licenses/onnxruntime-LICENSE.txt and
    licenses/onnxruntime-ThirdPartyNotices.txt
  occt-import-js 0.0.23 and the Open CASCADE Technology it is compiled from
    (app/occt/occt-import-js.wasm and occt-import-js.noeh.wasm, for the
    STEP preview), GNU Lesser General Public License 2.1 (Open CASCADE with
    its exception); the license texts are in licenses/occt-import-js-LICENSE.txt
    and licenses/occt-LICENSE.txt. The modules are separate files, loaded at
    run time, and may be replaced with others built from the sources:
    https://github.com/kovacsv/occt-import-js (v0.0.23) and
    https://github.com/Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT. server-go/scripts/occt/build.sh
    rebuilds them from the occt-import-js package with binaryen 132.
